issue.body:
Adds `home.services`, the home-manager analog to NixOS `system.services` for [modular services](https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/#modular-services).

Each entry is a `_class = "service"` submodule sourced from nixpkgs' `lib/services/lib.nix`, extended with the upstream portable systemd module (`nixos/modules/system/service/systemd/service.nix`). That means service modules already shipped with packages, e.g. `pkgs.ghostunnel.passthru.services.default`, drop in unchanged with the same `process.argv`, `systemd.service`, `systemd.mainExecStart`, etc. that NixOS sees. This service portability across module systems is the point of modular services, which their support in home-manager may help validate.

Lifted units are translated from NixOS-style attrs (`wantedBy`, `serviceConfig`, `unitConfig`, `environment`, ...) into the section-based INI shape (`{ Unit; Service; Install; }`) home-manager's `systemd.user.services` already consumes. Only common keys are mapped explicitly; uncommon options remain reachable via `unitConfig` / `serviceConfig` / `socketConfig`. Sub-services and their units are dashed under the parent service name; `process.argv` becomes the default `ExecStart` for the primary unit, which defaults to `WantedBy=default.target`.

`configData.<name>` entries are materialized under `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/system-services/<service-prefix>/<name>` (mirroring how NixOS lifts `configData` to `environment.etc`), with the absolute path injected back into `configData.<name>.path` so services can refer to their files at a stable location.

### Example

```nix
home.services."tunnel" = {
  imports = [ pkgs.ghostunnel.passthru.services.default ];
  ghostunnel = {
    listen = "127.0.0.1:8443";
    target = "127.0.0.1:8080";
    cert = "/run/secrets/cert.pem";
    key = "/run/secrets/key.pem";
    allowAll = true;
  };
};
```

Produces `~/.config/systemd/user/tunnel.service` with the expected `ExecStart`, `LoadCredential`, and `WantedBy=default.target`.

This change mirrors the surface of nixpkgs' portable systemd module (services + sockets only). Other unit kinds home-manager supports natively (timers, paths, mounts) are omitted in favor of staying on par with support on the nixpkgs side.

Disclaimer: i used a coding agent in the creation of this patch.

### Tested

Three nmt tests (`nix run .#tests -- home-services`):
- `home-services-basic`: `process.argv`-only service produces a unit with the expected `ExecStart` and install target.
- `home-services-configdata`: `configData` entry is materialized at the expected XDG path.
- `home-services-ghostunnel`: `pkgs.ghostunnel.passthru.services.default` drops in and produces a unit with the expected ghostunnel flags and `LoadCredential` entries.

## Checklist

- [x] Change is backwards compatible.
- [x] Code formatted with `nix fmt` or `nix-shell -A dev --run treefmt`.
- [x] Code tested through `nix run .#tests -- test-all` or `nix-shell --pure tests -A run.all`.
- [x] Test cases updated/added. See [example](https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/commit/f3fbb50b68df20da47f9b0def5607857fcc0d021#diff-b61a6d542f9036550ba9c401c80f00ef).
- [x] Commit messages are formatted like

  ```
  {component}: {description}

  {long description}
  ```

  See [CONTRIBUTING](https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/#sec-commit-style) for more information and [recent commit messages](https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/commits/master) for examples.

- If this PR adds a new module

  - [x] Added myself as module maintainer. See [example](https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/a51598236f23c89e59ee77eb8e0614358b0e896c/modules/programs/lesspipe.nix#L11).
  - [x] Generate a news entry. See [News](https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/index.xhtml#sec-news)
  - [x] Basic tests added. See [Tests](https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/index.xhtml#sec-tests)

- If this PR adds an exciting new feature or contains a breaking change.
  - [x] Generate a news entry. See [News](https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/index.xhtml#sec-news)

- [ ] optional: await NixOS/nixpkgs#507052, which could ensure a stable entry-point (to prevent a future breaking change over this)

